  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the interaction with HN through multiple pathways, with the most direct link emerging from the first path, which establishes a direct target relationship between Mollicellin N and NCI-H524, which is subsequently targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and finally by HN. This suggests a chain of molecular interactions where Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of a downstream target, potentially influencing HN through a series of biochemical steps. The second and third paths provide additional support, showing that Mollicellin N also targets A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets HN. These findings collectively indicate that Mollicellin N may exert its biological effects through a complex network of targets, with HN being a downstream effector in at least two distinct pathways. The integration of these evidence strands supports the hypothesis that Mollicellin N interacts with HN via multiple molecular mechanisms, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
